## General Rules

1. Always `COUNT(DISTINCT member_id)` — never double-count
2. Filter `primary_membership_id IS NULL` for core member counts
3. Do NOT filter by `status` for active counts
4. Active = `CURRENT_DATE <= end_date` (future starts count)
5. Exclude `test_account = true` from all reporting queries
6. Use views where available — they handle complex joins
7. Never hardcode values from `work_estimations` or `system_config`

